  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given that the function holds Rolle&#39;s theorem in the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Now, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>"
